# Schema validation rules

## Where schemas live
All Zod schemas live in `packages/shared-schemas`.
Do NOT create inline ad hoc schemas in route handlers or components.

## What must be validated
- All API request payloads (inbound)
- All API response bodies (outbound)
- All workflow config files on load
- All content bundle files on load
- All AI task outputs before use
- All analytics events before persistence

## Validation pattern
```typescript
import { SomeSchema } from '@ctcc/shared-schemas';
const result = SomeSchema.safeParse(input);
if (!result.success) { /* handle error */ }
```

## AI output validation
AI outputs must be validated with the matching output schema before being passed to the UI or persistence layer.
Failed AI output validation must trigger the fallback, not surface raw model text.
